    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in the `frai` CLI! The issue was that the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed through to the `frai-gate` executable.\n\n**The Problem:**\nWhen running `frai gate init --ci`, only the positional arguments (`init`) were being forwarded to the gate CLI, while the `--ci` flag was lost because it was being parsed by the root program but not re-passed to the subcommand handler.\n\n**The Fix:**\nModified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (line 753) to reconstruct the full argument list from `process.argv` instead of just using the parsed `args` parameter. This ensures all flags (like `--ci`) are properly forwarded to the frai-gate CLI:\n\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex >= 0 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : (args ?? []);\n```\n\n**Testing Confirmation:**\n\u2705 Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` and confirmed both files are now created:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\nThe workflow file contains the correct GitHub Actions configuration and will properly run the gate checks on every PR.",
